---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — LaunchPad"
  description="Why LaunchPad exists, who it is for, and how its content is written and reviewed."
  path="about"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container column">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Financial and business knowledge is usually passed down, not taught. If your family
        does not have it, school rarely fills the gap.
      </p>

      <h2>The gap</h2>
      <p>
        Most advice about starting a business or managing money quietly assumes a starting
        point: savings you can risk, a parent who has done it before, an adviser to call, or
        a network that opens doors. Plenty of people have none of those things, and the
        advice that does reach them is usually attached to something for sale.
      </p>
      <p>
        Across OECD countries, about 18% of 15-year-olds lack basic financial literacy, and
        access to financial education at school explains a meaningful share of the
        difference in scores. Meanwhile hundreds of millions of young people have a phone
        and a data connection but no one to ask.
      </p>

      <h2>What LaunchPad does differently</h2>
      <p>
        Everything here is free, written in plain language, and assumes you are starting
        from zero. Lessons use real numbers instead of theory, say plainly when something is
        difficult, and never recommend a product the site benefits from.
      </p>
      <p>
        Content is written to make sense internationally. Banking access, currency
        stability, and what counts as a normal income vary enormously between countries, so
        lessons explain the principle underneath rather than assuming one financial system.
        The calculators let you switch currency.
      </p>

      <h2>Who it is for</h2>
      <p>
        Roughly ages 15 to 21 — old enough to earn, start something, or make a financial
        decision that matters, and young enough that these habits have decades to compound.
      </p>

      <h2>How content is handled</h2>
      <p>
        Lessons cite their sources. Anything about money is education, never personalised
        advice: LaunchPad does not tell anyone what to buy, sell, or hold. Market examples
        use historical data rather than current prices. Contributors are credited by first
        name and country only, and writers under 18 need a parent or teacher to sign off.
      </p>

      <h2>The project</h2>
      <p>
        LaunchPad is a college passion project by Rajvir Dixit, extending the idea behind
        his school club, Business Lab: that business is a life skill rather than a
        specialism. It is built in the open and will stay free.
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href={`${base}/learn`}>Start learning</a> · <a href={`${base}/privacy`}>How your data is handled</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lede { font-size: 19px; color: var(--ink-2); }
</style>
